Dialogue: 1,0:00:18.50,0:00:34.30,CreditGraphic,,0,0,0,,Whip  @whipcampaigns\NMadeleine Rivera, Fox News\NSource: Fox & Friends Weekend, Nov. 22, 2026
Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.14,0:00:02.50,Default,,0,0,0,,So AAA projects about\N73 million people
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.50,0:00:06.15,Default,,0,0,0,,are expected to travel by car\Nfor the Thanksgiving holiday.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.19,0:00:09.25,Default,,0,0,0,,That is a drop of about 200,000\Ncompared to last year
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.25,0:00:11.09,Default,,0,0,0,,due in part to high gas prices.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.09,0:00:15.49,Default,,0,0,0,,But many are still choosing to drive\Nbecause it remains the cheapest
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.51,0:00:17.80,Default,,0,0,0,,and easiest way to get around.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.83,0:00:18.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Gas prices have dropped slightly.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.50,0:00:19.30,Graphic,,0,0,0,,Gas prices have dropped slightly.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.35,0:00:25.33,Graphic,,0,0,0,,The national average for a gallon of gas\Nis $3.64, down 18 cents from last week.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.81,0:00:30.61,Graphic,,0,0,0,,Crude oil has dropped to the low $80\Nper barrel range, helping decrease prices.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.05,0:00:34.30,Graphic,,0,0,0,,But the national average is still\N60 cents higher than last year.
